
Temperature, RTC, and OLED host tests
====================================

Run from the project root:

	pio test -e native -f test_ds18b20_monitor

In VS Code, use PlatformIO > Project Tasks > native > Advanced > Test.
The suite uses Unity and mock Arduino/OneWire/DallasTemperature/Wire/U8x8/U8g2/
ThreeWire/RtcDS1302 headers.
It runs on the PC and does not upload firmware or access a serial port.
test_main.cpp includes src/main.cpp, so test_build_src must remain disabled
to avoid compiling the firmware twice or using the real hardware libraries.

GCC and G++ must be on PATH. On this Windows machine, the installed MSYS2
UCRT64 toolchain is in C:\msys64\ucrt64\bin. No project-specific toolchain
script is required. The native -static flag avoids runtime DLL lookup problems
on Windows; other host toolchains may need different flags.

If IntelliSense reports missing C++ standard headers in the mocks while tests
pass, select the native PlatformIO environment and rebuild its IntelliSense
index. The Nano/AVR configuration is for firmware, not these host-only headers.
Do not edit PlatformIO's auto-generated c_cpp_properties.json by hand.

Coverage includes valid/invalid temperatures and min/max, conversion timing,
formatting boundaries, display absence and address fallback, I2C data NACKs,
short writes and timeouts, unchanged-frame suppression, bounded recovery, cache
reset, and 32-bit timer rollover. RTC coverage includes saved-time preservation,
charging disabled for CR2032, write protection, calendar boundaries and invalid
dates, bounded serial time-setting commands, write read-back, and clock operation
during sensor faults. UI bounds use approximate mock font widths, not real glyphs.
Button coverage includes debouncing, short/long SET actions, once-per-press
adjustments, field cycling and calendar clamping, safe save and failed-save state,
serial conflicts, cancel timeout, OLED loss, and timer rollover. Integration
tests check short presses are handled during asynchronous conversion, recovery
is deferred while editing, and field selection redraws immediately. The sensor
mock counts reads so early reads before the 750 ms conversion delay are detected.
The mock I2C driver intentionally mirrors U8x8's
unchecked endTransmission behavior so the checked project callback is exercised.

Build real firmware separately:

	pio run -e nanoatmega328

The Nano environment excludes this desktop-only test suite. Passing mock
tests does not verify physical wiring, sensor accuracy, or device operation.
